    <string name="website">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n  &lt;title&gt;HTTPS Page&lt;/title&gt;\n  &lt;script src=\&quot;http://emulator.xyz.com/static/script.js\&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n  &lt;link rel=\&quot;stylesheet\&quot; href=\&quot;http://emulator.xyz.com/static/style.css\&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;base href=\&quot;http://emulator.xyz.com/\&quot;&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body&gt;\n  &lt;h1&gt;Served over data&lt;/h1&gt;\n\n  &lt;h1&gt;Secure origin&lt;/h1&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;This page is served over HTTPS.&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    // check if secure context\n    if (window.isSecureContext) {\n      document.write(\&quot;&lt;p&gt;This is a secure context.&lt;/p&gt;\&quot;);\n    } else {\n      document.write(\&quot;&lt;p&gt;This is NOT a secure context.&lt;/p&gt;\&quot;);\n    }\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n\n  &lt;h1&gt;Upgradable Content&lt;/h1&gt;\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;Image src&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;img src=\&quot;/static/image.png\&quot; alt=\&quot;HTTPS image\&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;If you see HTTP, it is served over HTTP&lt;/p&gt;\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;Video src&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;video src=\&quot;/static/video.mp4\&quot; controls&gt;\n    Your browser does not support the video tag.\n  &lt;/video&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;If you see the earth, it is served over HTTP&lt;/p&gt;\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;Audio src&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;audio src=\&quot;/static/audio.mp3\&quot; controls&gt;\n    Your browser does not support the audio element.\n  &lt;/audio&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;If you hear a Miaow, it is served over HTTP&lt;/p&gt;\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;Audio source&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;audio controls&gt;\n    &lt;source src=\&quot;/static/audio.mp3\&quot; type=\&quot;audio/mpeg\&quot;&gt;\n    Your browser does not support the audio element.\n  &lt;/audio&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;If you hear a Miaow, it is served over HTTP&lt;/p&gt;\n\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;Video source&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;video controls&gt;\n    &lt;source src=\&quot;/static/video.mp4\&quot;&gt;\n    Your browser does not support the video tag.\n  &lt;/video&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;If you see the earth, it is served over HTTP&lt;/p&gt;\n\n  &lt;hr&gt;\n\n  &lt;h1&gt;Blockable Content&lt;/h1&gt;\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;Script src&lt;/h2&gt;\n\n  &lt;p id=\&quot;script\&quot;&gt;No script was loaded&lt;/p&gt;\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;Link href stylesheet&lt;/h2&gt;\n\n  &lt;p id=\&quot;style\&quot;&gt;If this is red, it is served over HTTP. If it is green, it is served over HTTPS. If it is black, it is blocked.&lt;/p&gt;\n\n\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;iframe src&lt;/h2&gt;\n\n  &lt;iframe src=\&quot;http://emulator.xyz.com/redir\&quot; width=\&quot;600\&quot; height=\&quot;400\&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;If you see \&#39;served over HTTP\&#39; in the iframe, it is served over HTTP. If you see \&#39;served over HTTPS\&#39;, it is served over HTTPS. Otherwise, it is blocked.&lt;/p&gt;\n\n\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;Fetch&lt;/h2&gt;\n   &lt;p id=\&quot;fetch\&quot;&gt;No fetch result yet&lt;/p&gt;\n   &lt;script&gt;\n    fetch(\&quot;/static/text.txt\&quot;)\n      .then(response =&gt; response.text())\n      .then(data =&gt; {\n        document.getElementById(\&quot;fetch\&quot;).textContent =\n          \&quot;Fetch succeeded over: \&quot; + data;\n      })\n      .catch(err =&gt; {\n        document.getElementById(\&quot;fetch\&quot;).textContent =\n          \&quot;Fetch blocked or failed: \&quot; + err;\n      });\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;XMLHttpRequest&lt;/h2&gt;\n   &lt;p id=\&quot;xhr\&quot;&gt;No XHR result yet&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    var xhr = new XMLHttpRequest();\n    xhr.open(\&quot;GET\&quot;, \&quot;/static/text.txt\&quot;, true);\n    xhr.onload = function() {\n      if (xhr.status === 200) {\n        document.getElementById(\&quot;xhr\&quot;).textContent =\n          \&quot;XHR succeeded over: \&quot; + xhr.responseText;\n      } else {\n        document.getElementById(\&quot;xhr\&quot;).textContent =\n          \&quot;XHR failed with status: \&quot; + xhr.status;\n      }\n    };\n    xhr.onerror = function() {\n      document.getElementById(\&quot;xhr\&quot;).textContent = \&quot;XHR blocked or network error\&quot;;\n    };\n    xhr.send();\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;CSS URL background-image&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;div id=\&quot;css-url-test\&quot; style=\&quot;width:200px; height:100px; border:1px solid black;\&quot;&gt;\n    CSS background test\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    #css-url-test {\n      background-image: url(\&quot;/static/image.png\&quot;);\n      background-size: contain;\n      background-repeat: no-repeat;\n      background-position: center;\n    }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;If the box shows an HTTP image, it is served over HTTP. If it shows an HTTPS image, it is served over HTTPS. If it is blank, it is blocked.&lt;/p&gt;\n\n    &lt;h2&gt;Object data attribute&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;object data=\&quot;/redir\&quot; width=\&quot;400\&quot; height=\&quot;200\&quot;&gt;&lt;/object&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;If you see \&#39;served over HTTP\&#39; in the iframe, it is served over HTTP. If you see \&#39;served over HTTPS\&#39;, it is served over HTTPS. Otherwise, it is blocked.&lt;/p&gt;\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;Navigator sendBeacon url&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;p id=\&quot;beacon\&quot;&gt;Beacon not sent yet&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;script&gt;\n    let beaconData = new Blob([\&quot;Beacon test data\&quot;], { type: \&quot;text/plain\&quot; });\n    let sent = navigator.sendBeacon(\&quot;static/beacon\&quot;, beaconData);\n    document.getElementById(\&quot;beacon\&quot;).textContent = sent\n      ? \&quot;Beacon send attempted over HTTP\&quot;\n      : \&quot;Beacon send failed (blocked or not supported)\&quot;;\n  &lt;/script&gt;\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;Image srcset&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;img\n    src=\&quot;/static/image.png\&quot;\n    srcset=\&quot;\n      /static/image-small.png 300w\n    \&quot;\n    sizes=\&quot;(max-width: 600px) 300px\&quot;\n    alt=\&quot;HTTP srcset test\&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;p&gt;If the image displays red, one of the srcset candidates was loaded over HTTP. If it displays green, it was loaded over HTTPS. If it is blank, it was blocked.&lt;/p&gt;\n\n  &lt;h2&gt;Web font&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;style&gt;\n    @font-face {\n    font-family: \&#39;CustomFont\&#39;;\n    font-style: italic;\n    font-weight: 300;\n    font-display: swap;\n    src: url(\&quot;/static/font.woff2\&quot;) format(\&#39;woff2\&#39;);\n    unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA, U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193, U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;\n}\n    #font {\n      font-family: \&quot;CustomFont\&quot;, sans-serif;\n      font-size: 20px;\n    }\n  &lt;/style&gt;\n  &lt;p id=\&quot;font\&quot;&gt;If you see Comic Sans, it was loaded over HTTP. If you see a colorful font, it was loaded over HTTPS. Otherwise, it was blocked&lt;/p&gt;\n\n\n  &lt;h1&gt;Others&lt;/h1&gt;\n  &lt;h2&gt;Links to other pages&lt;/h2&gt;\n  &lt;a href=\&quot;/redir\&quot;&gt;Link to other page emulator&lt;/a&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;\n</string>
